readme=f'''# Director creates the edit — 7 November 2026

[Watch the Director's 12-second result](Director%20-%20Travel%20in%20motion.mp4) · [Watch the real planning and native Apply](Director%20planning%20and%20native%20apply.mp4) · [Complete finished playback beside its editable timeline](Finished%20movie%20in%20Studio.mp4) · [Manual continuation](Manual%20continuation%20in%20Studio.mp4).

The actual Studio Director receives a brief, calls the installed local model, chooses three shots and creates 10 ordinary editable layers with 74 motion keys. It selects orbiting picture cards, a six-strip time weave and a full-frame ending. Review precedes Apply; native Undo/Redo, independent restore and changing one generated motion key all pass. The soundtrack was manually selected beforehand. This is a private early Director demonstration, not owner creative approval or a claim of unrestricted editing.

The downloaded movie is 12s / 288 frames / 24fps / 1280×720 H.264/AAC. Its SHA-256 is `{binding['movieSha256']}`. The matching native backup, exact storyboard, original source clips, original score, actual Studio recordings, UI stills and technical evidence are included. The new controls are installed only in the isolated local demo; production is unchanged.

The model works from your brief and clip metadata. It does not yet watch the videos, understand speech or choose music. Motion treatments come from four supported authoring recipes; this run exercises three. It adds an editable sequence over the beginning of the existing programme. The twelve-second source trim and score were set normally before planning. Broader autonomous sequencing, audio/scene understanding and creative quality remain unfinished.

Live playback reaches the end in {live['wallMs']/1000:.3f}s; finished playback takes {finished['wallMs']/1000:.3f}s. Observed recordings capture {capture['Live Studio playback']['observedCaptureFps']:.2f}fps live and {capture['Finished movie in Studio']['observedCaptureFps']:.2f}fps finished. Reported decoder drops remain {live['decoder']['dropped']} and {finished['decoder']['dropped']}; no whole real-time picture/sound guarantee or listening approval is claimed. Nine paused comparisons retain minimum diagnostic PSNR {picture['minimumDiagnosticPsnrDb']:.3f}dB, not a whole-parity pass.

`Editable Project.autopromote.json` is the exact post-export backup matching the saved render receipt. Its owned asset references require the retained isolated demo account/media for reopening. The original media and score are also copied in `Sources`. Authentication sessions are not included. Keep the earlier films and projects; none were deleted.
'''
